    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6ab7c26c-5b0d-5ff0-b44c-9c4d41f4bab6",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $CD=DC={I}_{2}$\n\n- **II.** $DE=ED={I}_{2}$\n\n- **III.** $D={C}^{-1}$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{2}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $DE=ED={I}_{2}.$ Computing $DE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
